## The Data Speaks: Over 750 Recalls This Year Alone

With 759 total recalls reported in 2026 so far, food safety is a pressing concern. Class I recalls, indicative of the most severe risks (e.g., health consequences like Salmonella or undeclared allergens), have reached 206 instances--signaling a problematic trend in production and oversight.

## The Repeat Offenders

Brands like "Spring & Mulberry Inc." and "Moonlight Packing Corporation" are on thin ice, with double-digit recalls and consistent involvement in Class I violations. Other notable mentions include "Ghirardelli Chocolate Company" and "Everpress Juice," whose scores hovering in the "F" range reflect poorly on their compliance efforts.

## Recent Recalls

Brand / Product / Reason

- "Joy Gourmet Foods LLC": Lassis (plain and flavored varieties) face recalls due to improper pasteurization, landing them as Class II.
- "Spring & Mulberry Inc.": Multiple chocolate products face Class I recalls for Salmonella contamination.
- "Utz Quality Foods, LLC": Several potato chip flavors were flagged for potential Salmonella presence.
- "Boichik Bagels, Inc.": Allergen mislabeling (undeclared sesame) on pumpernickel bagels resulted in a Class II recall.

## Takeaway

Check your pantry and follow up on recall alerts. Familiarize yourself with the brands that seem to recurrently struggle with food safety, as their track records may affect your purchasing decisions.
